            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic dissection of the anomalous-origin right coronary artery and left sinus of Valsalva.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E51-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anomalous right coronary artery arising from the left sinus of Valsalva is a rare congenital abnormality. Percutaneous coronary intervention of the anomalous-origin right coronary artery can be challenging. Iatrogenic aorto-coronary dissection is a rare and life-threatening complication. We present a case of aortocoronary dissection that occurred during angioplasty of the anomalous-origin right coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
